:{{Диалог}} There are a few things I'd like to ask.
::'''Jingyan:''' Mmm, go ahead. I'll do my best to answer.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} It seems to me that you're the most reliable person in the whole Chancery.
:::'''Jingyan:''' Mmm... I'm not at liberty to promptly respond to that question. May I ask, would you like to hear the formal response from a Realm-Keeping Commission officer, or the complaint from a regular staff member?
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} The formal response from a Realm-Keeping Commission officer.
::::'''Jingyan:''' All public officials at the Chancery have their own focus, and everyone is an integral member of the Realm-Keeping Commission.
::::'''Jingyan:''' I can only express my gratitude for your assessment as "most reliable," and would refrain from any comments on the other parts. Hopefully you can keep paying attention to and supporting the work of the Realm-Keeping Commission.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} The complaint from a regular staff member.
::::'''Jingyan:''' Yeah, your observation is not wrong. If you get lumped in with two other lazybones at work, you'll soon become the "most reliable" around the workplace, too.
::::'''Jingyan:''' It isn't a glorious title, so I simply couldn't be happy about it.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} I heard the official Dahao used to be in the Cloud Knights?
:::'''Jingyan:''' Mm-hmm... That's about Official Dahao's personal life. May I ask, would you like to hear the formal response from a Realm-Keeping Commission officer, or a personal gossip from me?
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} The formal response from a Realm-Keeping Commission officer.
::::'''Jingyan:''' Official Dahao's military experience in the Cloud Knights gives him a unique sense of responsibility. His intuition on the battlefield grants him a definite sense of purpose when dealing with issues big and small at the Realm-Keeping Commission.
::::'''Jingyan:''' Please trust in the professionalism of the Realm-Keeping Commission. Our officers come from different backgrounds, which only enriches our experiences and methods of dealing with complex social and public interactions. Pfft&mdash;
::::{{Диалог|Возврат}} What are you laughing at?
:::::'''Jingyan:''' We've all undergone strict training at the Realm-Keeping Commission. No matter how funny something is, we will never laugh, unless we can't.
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::{{Диалог|Возврат}} Are you doubting it yourself?
:::::'''Jingyan:''' I believe in the professionalism of every officer at the Realm-Keeping Commission, especially here in the Exalting Sanctum Chancery. Pfft&mdash;
:::::'''Jingyan:''' I'm sorry. I just thought of something funny. Tfft pfft&mdash;
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} A personal gossip from you.
::::'''Jingyan:''' Hmmm... You don't seem like the gossiping kind, so I'll tell you...
::::'''Jingyan:''' Actually, when Official Dahao was still a Cloud Knight, he saved my life. My admiration of him led me to join the Cloud Knights myself. I worked myself to the bone and eventually, I joined his elite squad.
::::'''Jingyan:''' Later on, General Jing Yuan was worried about him getting struck with early-onset mara due to his combat experiences and hoped he could accept a sinecure position as a Realm-Keeping Commission official in the Exalting Sanctum &mdash; and keep him from the pains of life and death.
::::{{Диалог|Возврат}} So he came to the Realm-Keeping Commission to slack off?
:::::'''Jingyan:''' ...Well, I don't think you can say that, as it's not exactly easy-going at the Realm-Keeping Commission.
:::::'''Jingyan:''' But judging by the results right now, he sure is idle. And I'm busier...
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::{{Диалог|Возврат}} Why are you here too?
:::::'''Jingyan:''' I applied for a transfer. General Jing Yuan let me come and be a minor officer at the Realm-Keeping Commission.
:::::'''Jingyan:''' I thought it would be great to help out Official Dahao, but as you can now see... I'm always putting in overtime with chores until midnight, which is far more than just "doing a solid" for someone.
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} You're behaving a little big for your britches.
:::'''Jingyan:''' ...It's business hours now. You're an Outworlder with an inquiry, and I am an officer of the Realm-Keeping Commission. Being disciplined is the expected work manner for a Realm-Keeping Commission officer.
:::'''Jingyan:''' How would you feel if public officials crack jokes and chat with you during work hours?
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} Your colleagues sure all love to.
::::'''Jingyan:''' ...
::::'''Jingyan:''' I will discipline them. Thank you for your attention and support to the work of the Realm-Keeping Commission.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} Keep up the great work!
::::'''Jingyan:''' There's nothing great about it. It's the least that we could do. Thank you for your attention and support to the work of the Realm-Keeping Commission.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} I've nothing else to inquire.
:::'''Jingyan:''' Sure.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The disaster is over, are you guys still busy?
::'''Jingyan:''' I think the workload is okay. The thing is, I'm always busy, whether there is a disaster or not... I guess that's why I can't feel any difference.
::'''Jingyan:''' It doesn't bother me, but I do hope that Official Dahao's schedule is less packed now... You know, considering his age and physical condition, it's easy for things to go wrong if he going hard at it.
::'''Jingyan:''' But he has a high self-esteem and refuses to accept that he's aged. So, I can only do some of his work for him secretly. As a Vidyadhara, this much work isn't going to force me into hatching rebirth.
::'''Jingyan:''' Hey, please don't tell him about this. I don't want him to worry about me.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I've nothing else to inquire.
::'''Jingyan:''' Sure.

;(Talk to Songyan)
;(First interaction)
::'''Songyan:''' Ah~ If the Realm-Keeping Commission could give me the cash directly and let me stay at home all day without doing this troublesome job, that'd be great.
::'''Songyan:''' Anyway, it doesn't matter what I do or not do, the results are always gonna be the same. Why not cut out this middle part...
::'''Songyan:''' Hm? Eavesdropping is rude, {{MC|ж=lady|м=sir}}, you know. What's up? If it's something important, please go to Official Dahao, and for literally anything else, please approach Officer Jingyan.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So... You just don't deal with anything?
:::'''Songyan:''' I'm the Realm-Keeping Commission's Most Intelligent, and I only show up when those two get stuck. In other words, I'm the Ultimate Trump Card. Do you lead with your ace when you're playing tiles?
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} There's only three officers staffing this tiny Chancery...
::::'''Songyan:''' What about it? There can be a trump card hidden among three people.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're just spouting nonsense, aren't you?
::::'''Songyan:''' There's a saying. "Of three people, one will be a slacker." If I call dibs on slacking off, then the other two can't.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What issues would you be handling normally?
:::'''Songyan:''' I'm the kind of person who hates inconvenience. If you have any kind of work that's not too tiring, not too troublesome &mdash; then I'm down for that.
:::'''Songyan:''' I'm the Realm-Keeping Commission's Most Intelligent, and I only show up when those two get stuck. Just look at those two, and I'm mainly talking about the Officer Jingyan here &mdash; still going at it so hard, so I don't have to.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I just so happen to have a really thorny problem that I could use your help with...
::::'''Songyan:''' No no no, any thorny problem should be handed over to Jingyan. She's the main backbone of the Realm-Keeping Commission.
::::'''Songyan:''' Have you heard of this saying before? "With little power comes little responsibility." The little refers to me.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm going to tell Officer Jingyan right now.
::::'''Songyan:''' Doesn't matter, mate. A person like her is born to work hard, and she never trusts what I do. Also, every time when there are "outstanding troubles" to deal with, she'll just complete it for me, personally.
::::'''Songyan:''' So telling her anything would just be adding to her troubles. I urge you not to do this.
::'''Songyan:''' *sigh* {{MC|ж=Miss|м=My man}}, put aside your judgmental look. I've put in the hours working long and hard before, and I was, once upon a time, considered an elite officer of the General Affairs.
::'''Songyan:''' Besides, why do I work at the Realm-Keeping Commission? If it weren't for my failed investments... With all the curves on the chart going down, and only the prices are going up. Working has become a necessary option.
::'''Songyan:''' I hustled, and I failed. Now, this is the best effort I can put into work right now.
::'''Songyan:''' Hey, don't leave just yet. As long as we're chatting here, there won't be any new tasks assigned to me. Let's chat a little longer, {{MC|ж=miss|м=sir}}.
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Songyan:''' Mystery novels are really popular around the Exalting Sanctum these days, right? Those armchair detectives crack cases just by sitting on their couch and following the story... I'd love to be an 'armchair officer' like them!
::'''Songyan:''' How's it going, {{MC|ж=miss|м=man}}? Got anything you'd like to talk about? Anything but work!
:{{Диалог}} Fine, let's chat for a while.
::'''Songyan:''' Thanks for doing that for me, {{MC|ж=lady|м=man}}. Let's talk about literally anything.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} So what do you actually get up to at the Realm-Keeping Commission?
:::'''Songyan:''' Based on my observations, Jingyan basically does everything. Dealing with fraud, riots, various emergencies, and criminal investigations. "When there's trouble, call the Realm-Keeping Commission" really is a common saying about the Xianzhou Luofu.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What do you mean based on your observation?
::::'''Songyan:''' That's just the conclusion I made from my day-to-day observations.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What do you do, then?
::::'''Songyan:''' As the Realm-Keeping Commission's Most Intelligent, naturally I engage in cerebral activity.
:::'''Songyan:''' Of course I get some work done. Residents with lost cats, dogs, aurumaton puppets, or missing household ingenia &mdash; that's my wheelhouse. I would apply for field work, and then check out the teahouse to investigate.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds very casual to me.
::::'''Songyan:''' Well, you know, investigations. I like to think chatting is also one form of investigating. Admiring the scenery is an investigation too. When you solve a case, you're praised &mdash; but if you don't, nobody even blames you. This is the kind of job I like.
::::'''Songyan:''' I might be lower in the Chancery's pecking order than even Diting, but I never lose courage. As long as I never try to live up to expectations, there's nothing to get mad about.
::::'''Songyan:''' If you hear about a rich lady who needs her dog walked all day, let me know. I can quit my job at the Realm-Keeping Commission any time.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Don't you have any sense of duty?
::::'''Songyan:''' That's such a serious accusation. I used to be a very responsible officer too. In fact, it's because I was too responsible that I paid a heavy price... Now, I don't dare take on any more responsibility.
::::'''Songyan:''' I might be lower in the Chancery's pecking order than even Diting, but I never lose courage. As long as I never try to live up to expectations, there's nothing to get mad about.
::::'''Songyan:''' If you hear about a rich lady who needs her dog walked all day, let me know. I can quit my job at the Realm-Keeping Commission any time.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} This Realm-Keeping Commission Chancery sure is a small place.
:::'''Songyan:''' After all, we only look after one zone.
:::'''Songyan:''' The Realm-Keeping Commission is the general affairs organization of the Xianzhou Luofu, and also the institution that engages with the public of Luofu most often. Every zone has its own Realm-Keeping Commission Chancery to keep up with the needs of citizens.
:::'''Songyan:''' There are many other Chanceries aboard the Xianzhou Luofu, and they're all pretty small in size, but large in amount.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} How have you not been fired yet...
:::'''Songyan:''' There's no need to be like that. I may not be diligent in my work, but I haven't committed any severe fireable offenses yet.
:::'''Songyan:''' Let me put it this way. Even Almighty Officer Jingyan has clashed with people who came for official business because she's not tactful enough. And that's where I come in, and things will go more smoothly.
:::'''Songyan:''' Everyone has their place in a place like this. Just let the gears turn as they do, and the chains pull as they do.
:::'''Songyan:''' I have heard some Outworlders talking about workplace culture back in their homeworld. Work attitudes like mine would have long been driven out of their version of Realm-Keeping Commissions. Ah, I do proclaim the Xianzhou Luofu to be a far superior place.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} That's enough chit-chat, then.
:::'''Songyan:''' Alright, if you have problems need solving, trouble Jingyan. And if you have time need killing, you're welcome to chat with me.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The disaster is over, are you guys still busy?
::'''Songyan:''' To be honest, it feels even busier than when things were at their most chaotic at the Luofu. I don't get it. How is it that after everything is over, I only find myself getting busier and busier...
::'''Songyan:''' Later on, I found out the reason. It was because Jingyan and Dahao were free enough to deal with me after the disaster ended.
::'''Songyan:''' Before, I could take advantage of the chaos and slack off a bit, but I actually have to do work now... Ugh, this is giving me a headache.
;(If {{Mission|Obsequies Performed, A Long Road Ahead|showChapter=0}} has been completed)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} That's enough chit-chat, then.
::'''Songyan:''' Alright, if you have problems need solving, trouble Jingyan. And if you have time need killing, you're welcome to chat with me.

;(Talk to Battuta)
;(First interaction)
::'''Battuta:''' Oh, so there is someone still willing to chat with this old coffin dodger... Ahem... When people get older, they can catch pneumonia just by having a sip of water. My aching aging throat...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you alright?
:::'''Battuta:''' Haha, they've already given me meds, so I'll just rest and recover...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Your body looks healthy. What's all this about...
:::'''Battuta:''' Dear {{MC|ж=girl|м=boy}}, you're far too optimistic. I may not even survive to see a complete recovery... *cough*...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Who are you?
:::'''Battuta:''' I'm Battuta. I used to be a judge in the Klimt Republic. My side job was a travel writer... But now, I'm just a criminal waiting around for the Sky-Faring Commission to repatriate me...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What are you doing here?
:::'''Battuta:''' Is it really strange for criminals waiting for repatriation by the Sky-Faring Commission to be waiting here? I'm Battuta. I used to be a judge in the Klimt Republic. My side hustle was a travel writer...
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Battuta:''' Are you back? Even though... *cough*... Even though you can only join me for a few moments, I still feel great about it. Tell me, to what do I owe the honor?
:{{Диалог}} I just want to chat with you...
::'''Battuta:''' Hahaha... *cough*... I thought people nowadays are just a bunch of heartless savages... Let's talk, maybe you can learn something from my short life...
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What kind of country do you come from?
:::'''Battuta:''' My homeland... The Klimt Republic is a great nation... *cough*... We have a vast territory, an efficient government, honest officials, and upstanding people...
:::'''Battuta:''' The Klimt Republic was said to be made from nothing by Akivili the Trailblazer when THEY established the star rail, leading my ancestors on THEIR path of exile to THEIR Eversummer Paradise.
:::'''Battuta:''' In gratitude for THEIR kindness, my ancestors selected warriors and embarked on trailblazing expeditions to transform dead worlds into living ones...
:::'''Battuta:''' About a millennium has passed since its foundation... *cough*... We've already seen seventeen star systems, with a vast territory, and rich products... That's why our nation needs someone like me: A Judge.
:::'''Battuta:''' Many planets exist in ecological environments different from this one... And so the prime minister and council... ahem... That is, our government needs judges like me to help ratify laws and regulations tailored to each of the differing local conditions...
:::'''Battuta:''' *cough*... When I was 20, I graduated from the Royal Academy of Laws, becoming a Doctor of Law at 24... A year later, I passed the qualification examination to become a judge...
:::'''Battuta:''' I can still remember... The prime minister at the time, Madam Wiesener, awarding me my medal and encouraging me to dedicate my life to the people of the motherland, just like her...
:::'''Battuta:''' Ahhh... How energized I was back then... The moment Madam Wiesener placed that medal on me, I felt like a carefree kid again &mdash; never to be tired again...
:::'''Battuta:''' That fantasy of vitality was so strong that it was only twenty years ago, when attending the state funeral of Madam Wiesener... That I realized for the first time that all of this would happen to me one day...
:::'''Battuta:''' Too old to handle official duties, too weak to handle continual interstellar travel, I ultimately lie here helpless on a hospital bed, desperately counting all the things I should've done but didn't, all those people I should've seen but hadn't...
:::'''Battuta:''' Hehe... That has twisted me into the kind of person I hate most, the kind who's loyal to their desires and gives no second thoughts to breaking the law...
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} You mentioned that you used to be a travel writer?
:::'''Battuta:''' I used to be a travelog writer... *cough*... Before coming to Xianzhou, I'd traveled all over the cosmos, experiencing all the customs and peoples of different star systems.
:::'''Battuta:''' I recorded these travel experiences in truth, put them into print, and immediately aroused enthusiastic responses...
:::'''Battuta:''' Actually, I have no misgivings... ahem... It's not due to any beautiful prose of mine, but rather because Klimt has always been like that... Any non-fiction writing is enough to rouse an impressed readership.
:::'''Battuta:''' The late Madam Wiesener, once said, "Whosoever has measured the soils of the motherland with their feet, is willing to spill their blood there." What she said is true... *cough*...
:::'''Battuta:''' I've seen new cities rise up on the richest planets... I've worked with nomadic herders on the poorest planets... I've seen the sun rise or set on every planet in my home system, and also the ebb and flow of every tide...
:::'''Battuta:''' In places where disasters rage rampant, I've fought against the local beasts with the farmers. On frontier segmenta, I've somehow survived combat against the Antimatter Legion...
:::'''Battuta:''' But all I've seen is still but a drop in the ocean... *cough*... My journey is not yet complete... But I will die soon with regrets... Am I greedy for longevity? Yes, but I'm greedier for the calling of a traveler.
:::'''Battuta:''' ...It's over, it's all over.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} And so you came to Luofu to experience longevity?
:::'''Battuta:''' You really are a quick one, aren't you... But please, let me start at the beginning...
:::'''Battuta:''' When I was in my early thirties... I once went to see the late Madam Wiesener... I told her I was going to run for prime ministry...
:::'''Battuta:''' I was still young back then, and brimming with exuberance... But Madam Wiesener shook her head and told me, "It's still early. Go to the human world, first."
:::'''Battuta:''' And then I went to the "human world"... And saw the field hospitals on the frontlines lacking doctors and medicine. I saw the farmers in the desert struggling to survive. I saw that not every young girl out there got to experience "a fair life"...
:::'''Battuta:''' I made a lot of promises back in those days, and I've been fighting to keep them to this day... But then I woke up from a long dream only to discover that I could no longer walk...
:::'''Battuta:''' Wait until you're old, and you'll find that your body is like an old grandfather clock that's gone wrong... At first, you think it just needs some oil, then the gears wear out, the mainspring loosens, and the pendulum loses its accuracy... *cough*...
:::'''Battuta:''' People are just like monkeys riding a unicycle while trying to juggle. While hurrying to catch those three balls up in the air, you still have to keep stepping on those pedals to spin the wheel and maintain balance...
:::'''Battuta:''' I'm old, and somewhat confused, but I remember every promise well... I'm afraid I'll never have time to fulfill them...
:::'''Battuta:''' That's why I've come to Xianzhou, because I have to be here... This is the only place where I can fight the ravages of time.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} I should go...
:::'''Battuta:''' Mmm, you go then. Don't waste your time here any longer with a criminal.
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I should go...
::'''Battuta:''' Mmm, you go then, quickly. Don't waste your time here any longer with a criminal.

;(Talk to Qingzu)
:'''Qingzu:''' (Trailblazer), I read the letter you obtained from the mara-struck.
::'''Qingzu:''' While the Cloud Knights were searching for the Stellaron's whereabouts, I was carrying out the general's orders &mdash; tracking down clues on the mara-struck. Thanks to your efforts, we now have a lead.
::'''Qingzu:''' To an outsider, this letter appears to be nothing more than good news detailing a recovery from a chronic illness. However, what is actually being discussed is a violation of the Ten Unpardonable Sins. It's heresy.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you talking about Merciful Medicus?
:::'''Qingzu:''' Correct. The term "Merciful Medicus" is one of respect &mdash; one that any law-abiding citizen of the Alliance would never dare utter.
:::'''Qingzu:''' It refers to none other than the enemy of the people of the Xianzhou &mdash; the one we now call the Plagues Author... The Aeon of Abundance &mdash; Yaoshi.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you talking about the pharmacological experiment mentioned in the letter?
:::'''Qingzu:''' That's right. Since the Alliance was first established, all medical practices aboard the Xianzhou adhere to strict standards that prohibit long-life or mutant modifications under the guise of "curing."
:::'''Qingzu:''' I went through all our files to find information on the experiment in question, and found nothing. I started thinking about how the Alchemy Commission's delve was sealed off... There must be an unspeakable secret locked away there.
::'''Qingzu:''' The author of this letter was likely the mara-struck you defeated. My guess is he was led astray and poisoned while under the pretext of being cured. You saw how he ended up...
::'''Qingzu:''' Such actions remind me of an organization that was eradicated from the Xianzhou a thousand years ago... the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus.
::'''Qingzu:''' They were disciples of the Abundance that sought to restore the way of immortality by unearthing a forbidden remedial formula.
::'''Qingzu:''' It's hard to believe a group that was wiped out so long ago would suddenly rear its head and create chaos once more. The Seat of Divine Foresight needs to learn all it can about this organization's status before the situation reaches a point of no return.
::'''Qingzu:''' If you come across any similar clues about the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus, come and find me at the Seat of Divine Foresight &mdash; these kinds of firsthand accounts are exactly what we require.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So, what do I get out of it?
:::'''Qingzu:''' Don't worry, the Seat of Divine Foresight always rewards those who contribute to our efforts.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds good to me.
:::'''Qingzu:''' Excellent. Your work will not be in vain. The Seat of Divine Foresight always rewards those who contribute to our efforts.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds like one big headache to me...
:::'''Qingzu:''' I understand, but all I'm asking is for you to keep an eye out when you have time. The Seat of Divine Foresight always rewards those who contribute to our efforts.
::'''Qingzu:''' I recently received some intel. It seems that certain individuals are taking advantage of the current chaos to lure in outworlders around Exalting Sanctum. Maybe you could start there?
::'''Qingzu:''' We sent an undercover investigator out a few months ago &mdash; they provided us with a rough idea of the situation.
::'''Qingzu:''' Unfortunately, it seems suspicions were aroused... We lost contact with the agent &mdash; I suspect he was discovered...
::'''Qingzu:''' You are a fresh face on the Luofu and an outworlder. I would feel more at ease if I could leave this matter with you.
:'''Qingzu:''' Danger is practically an inevitability, take care and try to stay out of harm's way.
{{Dialogue End}}

